  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Single IProvisioningHandler implementation registered in L2 DI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register in L2 control-plane, NOT BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth ceremony 21 MUSTs; App Service `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` MUST already be set to L2 UAMI resource ID BEFORE H4b writes KV-ref-shaped settings (F16 remediation gate). H4b's post-condition `/healthz` probe implicitly verifies this — if KV refs can't resolve, /healthz stays red.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Reuse background-job infrastructure; return 202; fire-and-forget.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key: appsettings-{env}-{manifestVer} — manifestVer is manifest hash from canonical-app-settings generator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Manifest schema per entry: `key` (App Service app-setting name with `__` for nested config), `source` (`kv-ref` | `per-env-input` | `literal`), `kv-secret-name?` (canonical), `per-env-key?` (interStepState lookup key), `literal-value?`, `iOptionsModule?` (documentation: which BFF module consumes this — for the IOptions binding audit report), `required` (bool, default true — required-and-missing = QuarantineRequired).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SINGLE batch write per run: build the complete diff → call `az webapp config appsettings set --settings k1=v1 k2=v2 ...` ONCE. NO per-setting calls. Rationale: each `az webapp config appsettings set` triggers an App Service restart; N calls = N restarts = N cold-starts = long unstable window. Batch = ONE restart.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Diff-first idempotency: read current app settings via `az webapp config appsettings list` → compute diff (missing + mismatched) → NO-OP if diff empty; otherwise batch-write ONLY diffing settings. Preserves manually-set operator overrides (e.g., diagnostic settings) — never clobbers keys not in the manifest.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Post-condition `/healthz` probe: after batch write + restart-wait, poll `https://{appServiceName}.azurewebsites.net/healthz` with backoff (30s / 60s / 90s / 120s / 180s = 8-min budget). Success = HTTP 200. Failure = QuarantineRequired with fail-fast diagnostic (parse the container docker-logs for the `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException` line → the module name is in the error; report it back to operator so manifest can be extended).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Per-env-input resolution: H4b reads `per-env-key` from Cosmos `interStepState` (prior-handler outputs). If a required per-env-input is MISSING (prior handler didn't emit it), fail startup validation BEFORE writing anything. This surfaces upstream handler gaps early rather than making them look like config drift.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">KV-ref resolution: for a manifest entry with `source: kv-ref` + `kv-secret-name: X`, H4b emits value `@Microsoft.KeyVault(VaultName={sharedVaultName};SecretName=X)` — vault name from Bicep parameter (env-scoped). H4b DOES NOT verify the secret exists on KV (that's H4-shared's job — H4b assumes H4-shared has landed per sequencing).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BINDING guard: manifest MUST NOT list Dataverse-ClientSecret or BFF-API-ClientSecret as `source: literal` OR `source: per-env-input` — those MUST be `source: kv-ref` pointing to canonical secret names. Manifest validation enforces this. Prevents an operator from accidentally writing a cleartext BFF client secret as an app-setting literal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md NFR-05">BFF /health must fail fast at boot on any Tier-1 IOptions misconfig — H4b's `/healthz` post-condition IS this check applied at H4b's timeframe rather than at boot. If /healthz fails, the manifest is incomplete + must be extended.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§10">L2 handlers register in L2 DI, NOT in BFF (§10 BFF Hygiene).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§11">NEW-surface justification field completed per §11 three-question gate (see &lt;justification&gt; below). H4b is a NEW handler primitive + NEW canonical manifest; both justified.</constraint>
  </constraints>

