  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a full manifest + all per-env-inputs present in interStepState + all KV-refs resolvable, when HandleAsync runs against an App Service with no prior app settings, then ALL manifest entries are written in ONE batch `az webapp config appsettings set` call; App Service restarts ONCE; /healthz returns 200 within warm-up window.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Diff-empty NO-OP: given current app settings == desired manifest values, HandleAsync performs 0 writes + 0 restart + does poll /healthz once as sanity check.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Partial-diff batch: given some current app settings match manifest + others differ or are missing, HandleAsync writes ONLY the diffing set in ONE batch call (verified via mocked writer receiving exact diff set).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Operator-override preservation: given an App Service app setting present but NOT in the manifest (e.g., `APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING` set manually by operator), HandleAsync does NOT touch it; only manifest-listed keys are managed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Required-per-env-input-missing Quarantine: given manifest requires `TenantId` per-env-input but interStepState doesn't have it, HandleAsync quarantines with "PerEnvInputMissing: TenantId (upstream handler H0 did not emit)" BEFORE any writes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/healthz-never-green Quarantine: given /healthz returns 500 for full 8-min backoff window, HandleAsync quarantines with parsed fail-fast diagnostic (module name extracted from container docker-logs via Kudu API).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BINDING guard: given a tampered manifest that lists `Dataverse-ClientSecret` as `source: literal`, IAppSettingsManifestReader fails validation with "BindingViolation: Dataverse-ClientSecret MUST be source:kv-ref" BEFORE any resolver call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-key match: two invocations for the same (env, manifestVer) — second call short-circuits before manifest read (`appsettings-{env}-{manifestVer}` match).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">KV-ref format correctness: for a manifest entry `source: kv-ref, kv-secret-name: AiSearch--AdminKey`, resolver emits value `@Microsoft.KeyVault(VaultName={sharedVaultName};SecretName=AiSearch--AdminKey)` — exact string match, no whitespace variance.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Generator determinism: two runs of Invoke-AppSettingsCatalogGenerator.ps1 against the same manifest produce byte-identical outputs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Generator IOptions binding audit report flags: (a) manifest keys with no corresponding BFF `.ValidateOnStart()` binding (orphan settings), (b) BFF `.ValidateOnStart()` bindings with no corresponding manifest entry (uncovered required config).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI; `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/` + `dotnet test` exit 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler catalog in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md` Step 3 enumeration includes H4b alongside H4 + H4-shared (main-session write).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sequencing verified: H4b runs AFTER H4-shared (task 200) + AFTER H4 (task 047) AND BEFORE H9 (BFF deploy) in the L2 state machine's handler DAG. Reason: H4b resolves KV refs → H4-shared + H4 seed the secrets; H4b sets app settings → H9 deploys BFF code that boots with those settings resolved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live-fire on Model 1 Prod: H4b executed against `sprksharedprod-api` writes complete manifest in ONE batch; /healthz returns 200 within warm-up window; BFF boots WITHOUT the F20 SIGABRT observed 2026-08-24.</criterion>
